blocks.explanation:
Kidney (renal) failure is a condition in which the kidneys lose their ability to filter wastes from blood and regulate fluid and salt balance.

(i) Acute kidney failure (kidney injury) occurs suddenly and often resolves with treatment. It may be due to:
1. kidney infection;
2. blockage in the urinary tract (kidney stones, bladder cancer or enlarged prostate);
3. certain medications such as NSAIDs;
4. blood clots in renal arteries or arterioles.

(ii) Chronic kidney failure develops over a longer period and is irreversible, so the kidneys cannot recover their function. The wastes must then be filtered from blood by artificial methods (renal dialysis: haemodialysis or peritoneal dialysis), or, in end-stage kidney failure, the non-functioning kidney is replaced by a healthy donor kidney (kidney transplant).
